The game-engine changes borg-rs carries in its Angband tree, so that our
engine is the engine borg-rs's core plays on (owner, 2026-11-14; docs/PILOT.md).

Not guarded: it changes the game on purpose. borg-rs 4.2.6-impact-v12 moved
its engine from upstream e473720 to upstream 42cd156ac (12 official commits:
the complete-rest flag on timed effects, the command-queue flush on deep
descent, the rest command's background marking, the terminal clear/fresh
split) plus its documented fork corrections (cmd-wizard.c). A stopgap: the
owner will extract that engine into its own repository, which every client
pins to, and this patch goes then.

Generated by tools/engine-patch.py from borg-rs 4.2.6-impact-v12 (e6d13fc)
angband/ (lib/gamedata and src), against our tree after patches 01-07:
the game data files that differ, and every compiled file's
difference, with borg-rs's recording hooks resolved away (BORG_RECORDING,
undefined in our builds) and without main.h (patch 01 guards the frontend's
declarations).
Regenerated at every re-pin (scripts/repin-borg-rs.sh). Apply with patch -p1
in the tree.

